---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';

// Drop a photo named abhi.jpg (or .jpeg/.png/.webp) into src/assets/ and it
// automatically replaces the "Photo coming soon" placeholder. No code edits.
const abhiModules = import.meta.glob<{ default: ImageMetadata }>(
	'../assets/abhi.{jpg,JPG,jpeg,JPEG,png,PNG,webp}',
	{ eager: true },
);
const abhiPhoto = Object.values(abhiModules)[0]?.default;
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={`About — ${SITE_TITLE}`} description="Who is Abhi Pandya? A 23-year-old UT Austin grad on a mission to see every country in the world." />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<div class="about-wrap">
				<header class="about-header">
					<h1>About</h1>
					{
						abhiPhoto ? (
							<Image src={abhiPhoto} alt="Abhi Pandya" width={800} class="about-photo-img" />
						) : (
							<div class="about-photo" role="img" aria-label="Photo of Abhi coming soon">
								<span class="about-photo-tag">Photo coming soon</span>
							</div>
						)
					}
				</header>
				<div class="about-body">
					<p>
						I'm Abhi Pandya. I'm 23, I just wrapped up my master's at UT Austin McCombs, and I've
						never been great at staying in one place for very long. So far that restlessness has
						turned into 30-something countries, more than 10 of them backpacked with everything I
						needed on my back. And the end goal is easy to say and a little crazy to actually do:
						every country in the world. I'm dead serious about it.
					</p>

					<p>
						But how I get there matters just as much as getting there. There's a difference between
						being a vacationer and being a traveler, and I think about that distinction a lot. I'm
						not trying to check landmarks off a list or stay somewhere comfortable just because it's
						familiar. I want the version of a place that most tourists never see. A few years ago in
						Vietnam, I spent two days moving through a cave system. Not the quick tour, an actual
						multi-day underground trip. That's the kind of thing I'm chasing: the stuff that takes a
						little more effort, a little more willingness to say yes to something unusual, and that
						never makes it onto a highlight reel.
					</p>

					<p>
						Even when I'm home, I need to be doing something active or I go a little stir-crazy.
						I've been hiking since I was a kid, I climb, I'm into extreme sports, and I just got my
						scuba certification, which basically opened up a whole second world to explore that
						happens to be underwater. Staying lean and fit isn't separate from the travel either.
						It's what makes it possible to move the way I do.
					</p>

					<p>
						Here's the other thing: I'm not trying to spend a lot to do this. Some of the best
						nights of any trip have been the cheapest ones, a family-run inn instead of the place
						with the reservation list, a walk-in counter instead of the spot everyone's heard of.
						You don't need a big budget to travel well. You need to be willing to go a little
						further off the route.
					</p>

					<p>
						So that's what this blog is. If you feel that same pull to actually experience the
						world instead of photographing it from a safe distance, you're in the right place. I'll
						write about the trips, the food worth going out of your way for, the trails, the dives,
						and whatever else ends up being worth talking about. No fluff, no sponsored roundups of
						the same fifteen tourist spots. Just what it actually looks like to go somewhere and
						mean it.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
<style>
	main {
		max-width: 1100px;
		margin: 0 auto;
		padding: 0 2em;
	}
	.about-wrap {
		padding: 5em 0 6em;
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 280px 1fr;
		gap: 4em;
	}
	.about-header h1 {
		font-size: 3rem;
		letter-spacing: -0.04em;
		line-height: 1;
		color: rgb(var(--black));
		margin: 0;
		position: sticky;
		top: 2em;
	}
	.about-header :global(.about-photo-img) {
		display: block;
		width: 100%;
		height: auto;
		margin-top: 1.5em;
		border-radius: 12px;
		box-shadow: var(--box-shadow);
	}
	.about-photo {
		margin-top: 1.5em;
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
		aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
		width: 100%;
		border: 2px dashed rgb(var(--gray-light));
		border-radius: 12px;
		background: repeating-linear-gradient(
			45deg,
			rgba(var(--gray-light), 0.35),
			rgba(var(--gray-light), 0.35) 12px,
			transparent 12px,
			transparent 24px
		);
	}
	.about-photo-tag {
		font-size: 0.75rem;
		font-weight: 600;
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: rgb(var(--gray));
		background: #fff;
		padding: 0.4em 0.9em;
		border-radius: 999px;
		box-shadow: 0 1px 4px rgba(var(--gray), 25%);
	}
	.about-body {
		max-width: 640px;
	}
	.about-body p {
		font-size: 1.05rem;
		line-height: 1.8;
		color: rgb(var(--gray-dark));
		margin-bottom: 1.75em;
	}
	.about-body p:last-child {
		margin-bottom: 0;
	}
	@media (max-width: 768px) {
		main {
			padding: 0 1.25em;
		}
		.about-wrap {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			gap: 1.5em;
			padding: 3em 0 4em;
		}
		.about-header h1 {
			font-size: 2.25rem;
			position: static;
		}
		.about-body p {
			font-size: 1rem;
		}
	}
</style>
